    <statement><p>Find a vector <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> that is perpendicular to the plane through the
points</p>
<p><CENTER>
<m>A = \left(-2,-1,3\right)</m>, <m>B = \left(5,-2,1\right)</m>, and <m>C = \left(-5,-3,-2\right)</m>.</CENTER></p>
<p><m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;v\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> = <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.
</p>
</statement>
    <hint><B>Hint: </B>If the vector is perpendicular to <em>two</em> vectors in the plane, it will be perpendicular to them all.  Can you find two vectors in this plane?
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;1,41,-17\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
